notes[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T17:18:27.515Z","harness:codex",Fold the compatibility repair into the benchmark/leaderboard tranche so the new command is exercised against the latest public SDK rather than the stale permissive range.
  "2026-08-20T17:42:16.514Z","harness:codex","Adopted @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20 exactly for development and >=2026.8.20 as the peer floor; updated the merge-driver marker to v2; removed obsolete manifest.pm compatibility metadata; raw-manifest compatibility now asserts zero findings. Current SDK strict dependency resolution required explicit allowUnresolvedDeps only in intentional dangling-edge fixtures. Metric reconstruction now requests unbounded note rows and token budget and refuses an omission envelope, fixing a 10,000-event false corruption under bounded default output."
  "2026-08-20T17:45:46.039Z","harness:codex",pm-changelog 2026.8.17 correctly refused the latest CLI bounded list-all receipt (5 of 45 items). pm-rl now passes explicit unbounded output budget and row limit in local and daily-release generation. The reusable default fix is tracked upstream at unbraind/pm-changelog#147; this workaround preserves fail-closed completeness rather than accepting a partial changelog.
  "2026-08-20T17:46:07.782Z","harness:codex","Latest strict health initially found pre-existing chain drift on pm-rl-81oc. The official history-repair dry run verified three entries would be rehashed, zero events discarded or reverted, and the pi-agent tests_add event preserved. Applied the audited repair; pm health --strict-exit now passes with only three non-gating provenance advisories."
  "2026-08-20T17:50:35.183Z","harness:codex","Fresh packed-artifact acceptance passed with @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.20 through both npm+npx and bun+bunx. Each disposable project initialized its own tracker, installed the tarball as a project package, and confirmed pm package describe exposed pm-rl benchmark and leaderboard commands."
  "2026-08-20T17:53:25.539Z","harness:codex","Privacy and repository-integrity audit covered the complete worktree, all reachable history, and two unreachable local commits: zero targeted credential/private-key patterns and zero private absolute host paths. GitHub reported zero open secret-scanning and Dependabot alerts. Code-scanning alerts were unavailable because this repository has no analysis, so that is a limitation rather than a clean code-scanning result."
  "2026-08-20T18:12:00.457Z","harness:codex","Accepted CodeRabbit workflow findings: release-date, release-tag, and repository-name expressions now cross the shell boundary through env; shared changelog completeness arguments are defined once in the Bash step. Behavioral workflow assertions cover the hardened contract."
